# BMW 1-series F20 five-door hatchback, 2011-2019.
#
# The second 1-series: the longer, wider rear-drive five-door with the
# reshaped nose and the more upright cabin. The three-door F21 is a different
# body and is not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_1_Series_(F20)
#
# Dimensions 4.324 x 1.765 x 1.421 m, wheelbase 2.690 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show the five-door in side, front and
# rear views; the side view governs.
#
# Colours: grade (c), BMW GB colours used on the F20 in its launch years:
# Alpine White, Jet Black, Glacier Silver and Deep Sea Blue. Weights 20, 18,
# 17, 15, total 70, provisional.
#
# Speed 220 km/h. Comfort 80/300, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 2011 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f20.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f20.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-1-series-f20/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the headlamp contours are too angular, and the side
# crease and Urban Line bumper inserts are understated. At 128 px the longer,
# wider five-door body and reshaped nose read as an F20 1-series.


obj=citycar
name=BMW1SeriesF20(AlpineWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=2011
intro_month=9
retire_year=2037
retire_month=6
speed=220
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=80
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=300

